# The base look against DGMNB on the chrome's pictures: the header, the
# sidebar, the calculator's rows, the History and Memory panel, the
# programmer's radix list, bar and bits (compare --batch D G --map chrome.map).
#
# The pictures: base GMNB (GMNB_THEME=base, GMNB_ACCENT=3b6fd8 =
# DGMNB_ACCENT) and DGMNB at 760x640, light and dark: standard, scientific,
# programmer; standard after GMNB_KEYS / DGMNB_KEYS '1234*56=789/3='
# (-keys); the sidebar open (GMNB_NAV=1, DGMNB_NAV=1: nav); Programmer with
# the bits (GMNB_BITS=1; DGMNB_CLICKS='62,260;600,500', its bit-keypad
# switch, then the pointer off it); standard at 360x600 (small).
#
# Excluded, as not the chrome's: the readout (widgets/display.rs); the
# keypad where DGMNB's cells fall on fractions of a pixel (Scientific and
# Programmer: five columns of 85.6 px; Standard at 360x600: rows of
# 61.3 px), whose labels widgets/keypad.rs places on GTK's whole-pixel
# grid; and the app's name in the sidebar's header (GMNB, DGMNB), which
# docs/theming.md excludes.
dgmnb-standard-d0 gmnb-standard-d0 exclude=8,50,444,116
dgmnb-standard-d1 gmnb-standard-d1 exclude=8,50,444,116
dgmnb-standard-d0-keys gmnb-standard-d0-keys exclude=8,50,444,116
dgmnb-standard-d1-keys gmnb-standard-d1-keys exclude=8,50,444,116
dgmnb-scientific-d0 gmnb-scientific-d0 exclude=8,50,444,104 exclude=8,260,444,372
dgmnb-scientific-d1 gmnb-scientific-d1 exclude=8,50,444,104 exclude=8,260,444,372
dgmnb-programmer-d0 gmnb-programmer-d0 exclude=8,50,444,84 exclude=8,282,444,350
dgmnb-programmer-d1 gmnb-programmer-d1 exclude=8,50,444,84 exclude=8,282,444,350
dgmnb-bits-d0 gmnb-bits-d0 exclude=8,50,444,84
dgmnb-bits-d1 gmnb-bits-d1 exclude=8,50,444,84
dgmnb-small-d0 gmnb-small-d0 exclude=8,50,344,116 exclude=8,204,344,388
dgmnb-small-d1 gmnb-small-d1 exclude=8,50,344,116 exclude=8,204,344,388
dgmnb-nav-d0 gmnb-nav-d0 exclude=8,50,444,116 exclude=47,10,78,26
